      'The beginning of the third week is a time of great vulnerability. Cells that will build the eyes, brain and face are already set aside in known places, so a toxin that kills cells now can delete a whole structure. Alcohol in high doses kills cells in the front of the midline and can cause holoprosencephaly, in which the forebrain fails to divide into two hemispheres, the ventricles merge and the eyes lie too close together.',
      'The danger is made worse by timing. Week 3 of development is about four to five weeks after the last period, when many women do not yet know they are pregnant and may still drink, smoke or take medicines. Other agents that can harm this stage include certain drugs such as thalidomide and retinoids, radiation, infections such as rubella, and maternal problems such as diabetes or folic acid deficiency.',
