      'Somites appear one pair at a time from the head end backwards at a steady rate, so counting them is a reliable way to tell an embryo’s age in its fourth week. In total 42 to 44 pairs form, named by region, though the first occipital pair and several coccygeal pairs disappear again. The remainder give rise to the vertebral column, ribs, sternum and skull base, the muscles attached to them, and the dermis over them.',
